    <link-summary>Documentation for the DORKAG plugins for JetBrains IDEs: AZD, JirAI, Codecov, QueryFlag and GBrowser.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Documentation for AZD, JirAI, Codecov, QueryFlag and GBrowser.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>DORKAG plugins for JetBrains IDEs: AZD for Azure DevOps, JirAI for Jira Cloud, Codecov coverage, QueryFlag query templates and the GBrowser web browser.</web-summary>

    <section-starting-page>
        <title>DORKAG plugins for JetBrains IDEs</title>
        <description>
            DORKAG is a set of plugins for JetBrains IDEs, built and maintained by Jonathan Gafner.
            The plugins bring Azure DevOps, Jira Cloud, Codecov coverage, database query templates and a web browser into the IDE.
            AZD, JirAI, Codecov and QueryFlag are paid plugins with a free trial; GBrowser is free and open source.
        </description>

        <spotlight>
            <card href="Azd.topic" icon="azd_icon.svg" alt="AZD plugin icon"
                  summary="Create and review Azure DevOps pull requests, track pipeline runs, work with boards and get AI pull request reviews in the IDE. Paid, with a 10-day free trial."/>
            <card href="JirAI.topic" icon="jirai_icon.svg" alt="JirAI plugin icon"
                  summary="Browse, create and edit Jira Cloud issues, move cards on the board and give your AI assistant Jira tools in the IDE. Paid, with a 7-day free trial."/>
        </spotlight>

        <primary>
            <title>More plugins</title>
            <card href="Codecov.topic" icon="code_cov.svg" alt="Codecov plugin icon"
                  summary="Codecov line coverage and pull request impact in the editor. Paid, with a 10-day free trial."/>
            <card href="QueryFlag.topic" icon="queryflag.svg" alt="QueryFlag plugin icon"
                  summary="Run saved database query templates on the text you select. Paid, with a 30-day free trial."/>
            <card href="GBrowser.topic" icon="gbrowser_icon.svg" alt="GBrowser plugin icon"
                  summary="A web browser in an IDE tool window. Free and open source (Apache-2.0)."/>
        </primary>

